  "goodToKnow": "Die Nachrichtenagentur is a news agency. Germany's largest is dpa (Deutsche Presse-Agentur, founded 1949, Hamburg/Berlin), whose reports supply most newspapers; others include AFP, Reuters and the church agencies KNA and epd. Reuters itself was founded by Paul Julius Reuter, born in Kassel. News reports often end with a source: (dpa). Die Nachricht means news item. Plural: die Nachrichtenagenturen."
